Licences of what the DA Privacy Kit AppImage bundles that brings none of its own into the
image, and where each text came from. They live in packaging/appimage/licenses of DA Privacy
Kit's source and are copied unchanged into usr/share/licenses/daprivacyscanner of the
AppImage (packaging/appimage/build.sh), beside:

  LICENSE        DA Privacy Kit's own (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  fallbacks/     the Ubuntu copyright file of each package the fallback libgirepository-2.0
                 and typelibs (usr/lib/girepository-fallback) came from, with SOURCES: the
                 snapshot of the Ubuntu archive their source is in, and how to fetch it
  pycairo/       pycairo's licences, from its own sdist (the wheel built from it carries none)
  proxy-tools/   from packaging/appimage/licenses (below): its sdist carries none
  sbom.cdx.json  what is in the AppImage, as a CycloneDX SBOM made from the locks

Every other Python package carries its licence in its .dist-info, which the build checks.
The texts in python/ and runtime/ were taken from the archives named here, checked against
the checksums given (the same pins as DA Assistant's AppImage, whose packaging/licenses holds
the same texts). When packaging/appimage/pins.sh moves to another Python or runtime release,
take them again from the new one: tests/test_appimage_packaging.py fails until the releases
named here are the ones pinned.


